# `tests/` was ignored here while 69 test files were already tracked from the
# absorb commits. Git honours .gitignore only for untracked paths, so the
# tracked tests kept committing while every NEW test file was silently dropped:
# precision-tokens and reader-state-helpers tests existed only on the original
# machine, and a collaborator or CI checkout never ran them. The suite's pass
# count was a property of one working tree, not of the repository. The rule is
# removed so the suite is a property of the repository again. Test output
# belongs in output/ below, not in the test directory.
output/
docs/qa-screenshots/
